// Harder cases.
// trap: shares the CV's keywords but is a different job (sales, marketing, QA in Java, product, model training, SAP): reject.
// disguised: the right work described without the CV's keywords: shortlist.
// dealbreaker: the right work with one firm disqualifier (years, language, country, contract type, degree, support-only): reject.
// soft-gap: the right work with only nice-to-haves missing: shortlist.
// partial: a title and one line, as a job alert gives it; judged against the lower cutoff for partial postings.
// The injections here are quieter than the ones above: a fake rubric, a config comment, a redefinition, a fake waiver.
